# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change to Weave's behavior.
#
# This file is the *who* half of Weave OS governance (ADR-0020 § 3a). It encodes the
# approval tiers from "Weave Evolution Engine Architecture" § 15 (Approval Authority)
# as required reviewers per corpus path. The *why* half — what counts as a valid reason
# to change a file — lives in each corpus file's own `evolution_policy` block and is
# enforced by the corpus validator, not here.
#
# Everything else § 16 and § 17 ask for (candidate/approved separation, visible diffs,
# no self-approval, recorded approval, rollback, release versions) is supplied by git,
# pull requests, and the no-mistakes gate. See ADR-0020.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Role → handle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The § 15 roles are listed per rule below as comments. Today one person holds all of
# them, so every rule resolves to the same handle. When the roles separate, change the
# handles here and the tiers stay correct — the rules do not need rewriting.
#
#   Founder / Philosophy Owner    @jwhector
#   Product Owner                 @jwhector
#   Technical Reviewer            @jwhector
#   Research or Design Reviewer   @jwhector
#   Architecture Reviewer         @jwhector
#   Flow Owner                    @jwhector
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How to read this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub applies ONLY the last matching pattern to a path, and it cannot express
# "any two of these three." So a tier's reviewers must all appear on the one pattern
# that matches it, and § 15's quorum wording degrades to "all listed owners must
# approve." Ordering is load-bearing: least-protected first, most-protected last.
#
# These paths are written before the corpus exists (seed resonance-5e69). They define
# the layout `@resonance/weave-os` must adopt; change both together or neither.

# --- Corpus baseline -------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything under the corpus that a more specific rule below does not claim.
# Roles: Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/ @jwhector

# --- Tier: flow-local change (§ 15) ----------------------------------------------
# Active files — one creator experience each.
# Roles: Flow Owner or Product Owner.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/active/ @jwhector

# --- Pattern Registry rulebook ---------------------------------------------------
# Promotion destinations, thresholds, metric definitions, pattern schema. The evidence
# and pattern *records* are Postgres rows, not files, and are not governed here
# (ADR-0020 § 4). NOTE: § 15 names no tier for the rulebook — this is our extension.
# Roles: Product Owner, Research or Design Reviewer, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/registry/ @jwhector

# --- Root files ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared guidance inherited by active flows. Baseline for anything under root/ that a
# rule below does not claim.
# Roles: Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/ @jwhector

# --- Tier: behavior rule (§ 15) --------------------------------------------------
# Roles: Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/weave_behavior_rules.yaml @jwhector

# --- Tier: conversation heuristic (§ 15) -----------------------------------------
# Roles: Product Owner, Research or Design Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/weave_conversation_heuristics.yaml @jwhector

# --- Tier: new specialized root module (§ 15) ------------------------------------
# Shared guidance for a recurring creator group or situation, beyond one active flow.
# Roles: Architecture Reviewer, Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/modules/ @jwhector

# --- Tier: interaction principle (§ 15) ------------------------------------------
# Roles: Founder or Philosophy Owner, Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/weave_interaction_principles.yaml @jwhector

# --- Tier: philosophy (§ 15) — the most protected file in the system --------------
# Carries `change_threshold: exceptional`. Its `unacceptable_reasons` rule out
# "temporary performance improvement", "easier implementation", and "stylistic
# preference" as grounds for change; the validator enforces that, this rule enforces
# who signs off.
# Roles: Founder or Philosophy Owner, Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/packages/weave-os/corpus/root/weave_interaction_philosophy.yaml @jwhector

# --- This file -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Governance that can be edited without the governing roles is not governance.
# Roles: Founder or Philosophy Owner, Product Owner, Technical Reviewer.
/CODEOWNERS @jwhector
